At 11:16 PM 07/18/2001 -0400, Craig wrote:
>On the ui thing, Lojbab's mention of the modifiers is not sufficient to
>capture the possible uses of UI.
>Is 'physical love' the kind where you cuddle a lot, the kind where you have
>lots of sex (like the greek eros), both,

I would presume either, possibly with an intensity marker, maybe with an 
exertion/effort indicator for the more active sort and a "comfort" 
indicator for the cuddling.

>  or something else? What is 'mental
>love' - amourous thoughts or love of knowledge?

A love expressed primarily through mental activity.  This might range from 
Don Quixote's love for his ideal lady to the mental recollection of the 
cuddling and /or sex of the previous example.

>  What is social happiness? If
>these are to be useful they need more clarification.

The Greeks elaborated their theories of love over centuries.  You want a 
Lojban science of emotions to appear in moments.  Use the language and your 
usage will come to embody that clarification.

